{
  "startedAt": "2026-10-16T01:36:35.792Z",
  "steps": [
    "Existing audio JSON opens the independent native-backed editor. Existing cues are rebound to other declared tracks and reordered without changing their identities. Inputs and equal-time stop-before-play order survive Chinese/English/Japanese at 390px with visible return/cancel/review/apply controls; review and Cancel leave both the draft and author tree unchanged.",
    "Apply changes only the ordinary unsaved source draft. Ordinary Save updates exactly the reviewed audio JSON; metadata, scene, referenced WAV and other author files remain byte-identical.",
    "Saved cue IDs and new track bindings survive reopening with the exact list order. Shared Rust sampling at 0.25 seconds confirms the music track is playing because its stop precedes play at the same timestamp.",
    "The same scene plans, builds and runs through real Godot. The host validates three audio commands (effect play at 0s, music stop then play at the same 0.25s timestamp) and independent audio/actor completion.",
    "Chrome downloads the generated engine project ZIP. Independent verification confirms one deduplicated WAV resource, extraction preserves its exact bytes and settings, and fresh Godot import/run at another path produces identical audio events."
  ],
